  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Heat will be the name of the game over the next few \ndays as the Bermuda high centered off the coast will slide S'wards \ntowards the Gulf Coast States while a thermal trough remains \nover the Piedmont. This will keep low level flow generally SW to\nW over the next several days. As a result, some weak WAA will \nallow low level thicknesses to increase closer to 1430m. Based \noff the offices climatological study this is forecast to result \nin highs in the low to mid 90s across the inland areas and upper\n80s to low 90s along the OBX and coast into the end of the week\nbefore a front impacts the region resulting in cooler \ntemperatures late week into the weekend. The hottest days will \nbe on Tue through Thurs. With dewpoints forecast to range from \nthe lower 70s to upper 70s will result in heat indices around \n95-104F this afternoon and again on Mon with heat indices closer\nto 100-110F on Tue through Thurs resulting in a chance for heat\nheadlines later this week. Lows each night will be in the 70s \nwhich won't provide much relief from the heat either. Even if we\ndon't reach official criteria in the coming days it will be hot\nand humid resulting in ENC reaching major heat risk thresholds \non Monday with some of the area potentially seeing extreme heat \nrisk levels Tue/Wed. We encourage anyone planning on spending \nalot of time outdoors this week to take proper precautions and \nstay hydrated. \n   \nOtherwise, a typical summer time pattern will be in place through \nmuch the week. Near zonal flow aloft with a series of shortwave \ntroughs pushing across the area will result climo precip chances for \nthe next several days with best chances through peak heating and \nseabreeze related for the most part but will also depend on timing \nand exact location of individual shortwave troughs. The severe \nthreat appears minimal for the next few days with limited shear, \nthough somewhat better shear develops toward the middle of the week. \nWe do look to have increased precipitation chances closer to Fri \nand into next weekend with the approach of an incoming cold front.",
